WEBVTT

00:07:29.236 --> 00:07:30.836
And so I had to just accept

00:07:30.876 --> 00:07:33.076
that certain people
aren't going to get it.

00:07:33.116 --> 00:07:36.236
I think the other thing I might do
is explain how it made me feel.

00:07:36.236 --> 00:07:38.476
You know, "that really hurts me because"

00:07:38.516 --> 00:07:40.596
and "I need you to understand
what that does

00:07:40.596 --> 00:07:42.876
and what you're suggesting
in those words."

00:07:42.916 --> 00:07:44.796
And so I might have better responses.

00:07:44.836 --> 00:07:48.276
I really encourage women and everybody
to have responses in the moment,

00:07:48.316 --> 00:07:50.316
because we're all going to face situations

00:07:50.356 --> 00:07:52.716
where someone says something
inappropriate at work

00:07:52.756 --> 00:07:55.716
or says something inappropriate
to someone else in front of us,

00:07:55.756 --> 00:07:57.796
and I want us to all have words around it.

00:07:57.836 --> 00:08:00.356
Another big idea in the book
is this idea of scarcity,